## T1-sway — the two numbers that did not mean what they looked like (19.09, build 3f93bfc4)

Instrumentation only, zero physics change, and the last open item of T1 is closed: the
apple's sway and pinning numbers are now measured over windows that mean something, and
there is a run in which the WIND IS SWITCHED OFF.

- `PlantBase.windOffSeconds` (0 = old behaviour) + a gate in `TreeBase.FixedUpdate`;
  `-appleWindUntil <s>` in `HeadlessTrial.BuildAppleScene` sets it. With the switch at 0 the
  wind force is issued on exactly the steps it was before — proven, not asserted.
- `AppleTrialRecorder` keeps every old key and adds: `swayFixedTipAmpM`, `swaySettledAmpM`,
  `swaySettledPkPkM` (one tip segment, chosen once at the first sample and followed; the
  settled window is t >= 4 s), `worstJointPinnedTimeFraction`, `hingePinnedJointCount`,
  `maxHingeOverrunDeg`, `windOnMaxAbsJointAngle`, `windOffMaxAbsJointAngle`,
  `residualAbsJointAngleDeg`, `residualTrunkLeanDeg`, `residualTipDxM` (last second of the
  run). The window definitions and the chosen tip index live in `build:`, never in the run
  block. `tree-const-assert.py` declares `windOffMaxAbsJointAngle` 0 on a run with no
  `-appleWindUntil`.

Measured (`apple_t1sw_*` fp `3f93bfc4…` vs `apple_t1sw_base_*` fp `94f41860…`, same
sources, one player each side): 28 of 28 physics run-block keys bit-identical on hold AND
on wind 0.12; the oak (`tree_t1sw_*`) reproduces its accepted canon (0.00103 / 34.17341 /
crownDrop 0.2553246 / pinned 0.20). Only `wallPerSim` and `sourceFingerprint` move.

What the honest windows say:

- `swayAmpM` 0.1465 m at wind 0.12 was a STARTUP TRANSIENT: the settled window (4-8 s)
  gives `swaySettledAmpM` 0.0222 m, peak-to-peak 0.0396 m. The stable tip id reproduces
  `swayAmpM` exactly here (0.1465347), so the contamination the audit feared is the window,
  not a swapped segment. The apple's steady sway is 2.2 cm — below the 0.10-0.30 m the
  acceptance wants, and that is a T4/T5 input, not a T1 one.
- Pinning is JOINT J08 (one order-1 limb): `worstJointPinnedTimeFraction` 0.683 in the hold,
  0.296 at wind 0.12, 0.559 with the wind off at 4 s — it sits 0.674 deg OUTSIDE its own stop
  in still air. `maxHingeOverrunDeg` reaches 2.066 deg under wind: the stops are soft. So
  `hingePinnedFraction` 0.0667 really is 1 joint of 15, and "pinned = 0" is not met.
- Wind off at 4 s (`apple_t1sw_windoff`): the deviation peaks at 6.4481 deg in the release
  window (0.1 deg past the wind-on peak 6.3525), then decays to 5.6541-5.6933 deg over the
  last second, against 5.6605-5.6713 for the no-wind hold run — residual **0.0220 deg**,
  crown tip back within **0.0007 m**. Mean |dAngle|/step falls 10x (0.00077 → 0.00004) while
  the wind-on run keeps 0.0002-0.0009. The crown decays back to rest when the driver stops.

